# SYMindX implementation

- Work on main. Preserve unrelated edits. The orchestrator owns Git integration.
- packages/runtime is the supported v0.1 core: Bun, SQLite, independent strict TypeScript contracts, character schema 1, explicit tools, echo or OpenAI-compatible provider, local authenticated API.
- mind-agents contains experimental legacy modules undergoing migration. Website demonstrations are not deployed runtime services. Do not equate legacy advertised capabilities with supported behavior.
- Use GPT-6 Luna coding fleets and the dynamic queue in docs/modernization/workflow.json. Each writer owns exact paths. Reuse completed findings; start the next implementation task when a slot opens.
- Provider SDK types belong behind adapters. Parse external and persisted JSON as unknown and validate it before use. Use role/event/config unions to make invalid states unrepresentable.
- Inspect scripts before validation. Use explicit no-env-file and ignore-scripts dependency installs. Compile, format and build as authorized; tests or behavior probes require an explicit request.
- No live provider calls, messaging, deployments, production data mutation or global install side effects.

Current commands and limits: packages/runtime/README.md. Historical guidance: docs/legacy/cursor.
